! =============================================================================
! AMPS Earth validation C9 GRIDDED branch: PAMELA global-shell cutoff validation
!
! Scientific observable
! ---------------------
! Adriani et al. (2016) Supporting Information Table S1 reports the magnitude
! of the proton cutoff AACGM latitude for seven rigidity bins.  Each timestamp
! is the middle of one 94-minute PAMELA interval.  C9 does not attempt to
! reconstruct the proprietary Resurs-DK1 attitude/ephemeris.  Instead, it makes
! a public-data global-shell comparison at PAMELA's representative altitude:
!
!   * one 475-km geodetic shell;
!   * vertically incident protons;
!   * IGRF + T05/TS05 driven by the bundled five-minute C9 driver;
!   * selectable FULL_SCAN or DIRECT_ACCESS numerical products;
!   * FULL_SCAN uses PENUMBRA_SCAN, retains Rc diagnostics, and additionally
!     classifies the seven exact PAMELA rigidities on the complete shell;
!   * DIRECT_ACCESS traces only those seven rigidities within a selected
!     absolute geodetic-latitude band;
!   * both products are filtered to the same band and reduced by the identical
!     longitude-averaged, hemisphere-resolved T=0.5 Python postprocessor;
!   * Rc_lower, Rc_effective, and Rc_upper remain full-scan diagnostics only.
!
! This is the Mode3D/GRIDDED companion to AMPS_PARAM_C9_gridless.in.  Both
! branches use exactly the same event driver, epochs, shell geometry, rigidity
! bracket, particle mover, trajectory limits, and postprocessing.  The only
! physical/numerical distinction is magnetic-field evaluation: this branch
! first samples IGRF+T05 on the standalone Mode3D AMR mesh and then evaluates
! the field along trajectories through the interpolation stencil.  Comparing
! both branches isolates mesh/interpolation sensitivity from the PAMELA test.
!
! The Python runner copies this template into every snapshot directory and
! changes only named directives (EPOCH, DRIVER_FILE, cutoff product, explicit
! rigidity list/access latitude band, scan count, shell spacing, rigidity bracket,
! trace time, and Mode3D mesh controls). The generated input
! and complete launch command are archived with every result.
! =============================================================================

#CALCULATION_MODE
CALC_TARGET             CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
FIELD_EVAL_METHOD       GRID_3D

#CUTOFF_RIGIDITY
! Default bracket 0.30-1.35 GV for protons.  The corresponding kinetic-energy
! limits are written explicitly because the AMPS cutoff parser accepts energy.
CUTOFF_EMIN             46.7936514838217
CUTOFF_EMAX             705.763955063706
CUTOFF_MAX_PARTICLES    1
CUTOFF_NENERGY          50
CUTOFF_SAMPLING         VERTICAL
! FULL_SCAN uses PENUMBRA_SCAN and CUTOFF_UPPER_SCAN_N, then independently
! classifies every exact rigidity below and writes a companion PAMELA-access file.
! DIRECT_ACCESS changes the algorithm to RIGIDITY_LIST and traces only this list.
! The C++ latitude filter is applied only by DIRECT_ACCESS, while FULL_SCAN keeps
! the complete shell. The Python T50 reducer filters both access products to the
! same bounds, so the primary scientific comparison uses an identical domain.
CUTOFF_SEARCH_ALGORITHM PENUMBRA_SCAN
CUTOFF_UPPER_SCAN_N     160
CUTOFF_RIGIDITY_LIST_GV 0.423556372,0.498397432,0.587877538,0.692820323,0.817006732,0.962081078,1.131017241
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MIN 35.0
CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MAX 75.0
CUTOFF_SCAN_SPACING     LINEAR
CUTOFF_TRACE_POLICY     ACCURATE
CUTOFF_BACKTRACE_CHARGE REVERSED
CUTOFF_TRACE_LIMIT_POLICY FORBIDDEN
CUTOFF_MAX_TRAJ_TIME    20.0

#PARTICLE_SPECIES
SPECIES                 PROTON
CHARGE                  1
MASS_AMU                1.007276466621

#BACKGROUND_FIELD
! The driver table is sampled once at EPOCH for each standalone snapshot run.
! The runner uses the checksum-verified driver bundled under C9/data by default.
FIELD_MODEL             T05
EPOCH                   2006-12-15T03:03:00
DRIVER_FILE             ts05_driver.txt
! Static values are parser-safe fallbacks only.  A loaded driver overrides them.
DST                     -100.0
PDYN                    4.0
IMF_BX                  0.0
IMF_BY                  0.0
IMF_BZ                  -5.0
SW_VX                   -450.0
SW_N                    5.0
T05_W1                  0.0
T05_W2                  0.0
T05_W3                  0.0
T05_W4                  0.0
T05_W5                  0.0
T05_W6                  0.0


#MODE3D_MESH
! Near-Earth resolution controls interpolation accuracy where the 475-km
! cutoff boundary is determined.  The outer-boundary target controls the cost
! of filling the +/-25-Re domain.  The default 0.02-Re near-Earth target is the
! production starting point; repeat C9 with 0.01 Re for mesh convergence.
MODE3D_MESH_RES_EARTH_RE     0.02
MODE3D_MESH_RES_BOUNDARY_RE  2.0
MODE3D_MESH_COARSENING       LINEAR
MODE3D_MESH_EXPONENT         1.0

#DOMAIN_BOUNDARY
! Bare lengths are kilometers.  +/-25 Re is large enough for the empirical
! magnetosphere used by this event-level access calculation.
DOMAIN_X_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_X_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Y_MAX             159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MIN            -159280.0
DOMAIN_Z_MAX             159280.0
R_INNER                  6371.2

#SPECTRUM
! Required by the common parser; not used by cutoff-rigidity tracing.
SPECTRUM_TYPE           POWER_LAW
SPEC_J0                 1.0
SPEC_GAMMA              2.0
SPEC_E0                 1000.0
SPEC_EMIN               1.0
SPEC_EMAX               2000.0

#OUTPUT_DOMAIN
! FULL_SCAN evaluates this complete geographic shell. DIRECT_ACCESS preserves
! the same structured shell definition but the Mode3D scheduler launches
! trajectories only at nodes within CUTOFF_ACCESS_ABS_LAT_MIN/MAX. The runner
! transforms retained points to AACGM at the exact snapshot epoch.
! SHELL_GEOMETRY=GEODETIC follows the current Earth cutoff-test convention.
OUTPUT_MODE             SHELLS
SHELL_COUNT             1
SHELL_ALTS_KM           475.0
SHELL_LON_RES_DEG       30.0
SHELL_LAT_RES_DEG       2.0
SHELL_GEOMETRY          GEODETIC

#OUTPUT_OPTIONS
OUTPUT_COORDS           GEO

#NUMERICAL
DT_TRACE                0.2
ADAPTIVE_DT             T
MAX_STEPS               500000
MAX_TRACE_TIME          20.0
MAX_TRACE_DISTANCE      400.0
TRAP_DETECTION          T

!#END
